----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SURFACE IMPLEMENTATION
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The feature view's six tiles — Total Readings, Avg Torque, Peak Power, Peak Regen, Avg Power and
Avg Motor Temp — reproduce the web SummaryStats data, composition and i18n keys (dynamics.totalReadings,
dynamics.avgTorque, dynamics.peakPower, dynamics.peakRegen, dynamics.avgPower, dynamics.avgMotorTemp; all
six already present in apps/shared/i18n/catalog/{en,he,ar}.json). Each tile maps to the shared TsStatCard
(web <StatCard>) with its Segoe Fluent accent glyph (the native mapping of the web lucide icon).

The native surface owns the motor-history read the web Driving-Dynamics page derives motorStats from
(useMotorHistory(vehicleId, 200) -> computeMotorStats): MotorSummarySource streams GET /motor (generated
operation get_api_v1_motor, scoped by vehicle_id + limit=200) through the shared CacheThenNetworkEngine;
MotorStats.Compute is a verbatim port of helpers.ts computeMotorStats (per-axle torque sum, per-row hottest
motor temperature, power/regen extrema, high-torque %); MotorSummaryProjection renders each value with the
web fmtNumber(x,1) precision and converts the Avg Motor Temp tile to the user's unit at the render boundary
(UnitFormatters.FormatTemperature, web useUnits) — verified "49.0°C" / "120.2°F", never a doubled "°°"
(the web SummaryStats.test.tsx temperature-suffix regression).

Every state renders (none hidden): loading skeleton tiles, the populated entrance-faded grid (native mapping
of the web StaggerContainer/StaggerItem), a friendly empty surface (web motorStats === null), an explicit
retry surface on hard failure, plus stale and offline freshness chips. Data binds through the shared P1/S8
state-holder (IMotorSummarySource -> SummaryStatsViewModel); the view performs no HTTP. Every tile and the
header chips carry Narrator names; the surface exposes a Group automation peer. Diagnostics emit
view.opened slug=SummaryStats (PII-safe).

Naming: a pre-existing sibling surface (SummaryStatsGrid, web charging-curve) had already taken the generic
SummaryStats* type names in TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews (SummaryStatsState, SummaryStatCard, SummaryStatsDisplay,
SummaryStatsProjection, SummaryStatsResultMapper, SummaryStatsRegistration, SummaryStatsDiagnostics,
ISummaryStatsSource, SummaryStatsSource, SummaryStatsJson). To avoid collisions the view class is SummaryStats
(free) and the support types use the MotorSummary* prefix plus the domain records MotorStats / MotorStatsSample.

